{"name":"Starboard","hex":"#016c4f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"starboard","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The right-hand side of, originally, a ship or other marine vessel, and now also an aircraft or spacecraft, when one is facing the front, or the bow or fore.","One of the two traditional watches aboard a ship standing a watch in two."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["On or towards the right-hand side of a ship or other marine vessel, aircraft, or spacecraft when one is facing the front; right."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/starboard"}],"entries":[{"title":"Port and starboard","blocks":[{"text":"Port and starboard are nautical terms for watercraft, aircraft and spacecraft, referring respectively to the left and right sides of the vessel, when aboard and facing the bow (front)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Aft_%28PSF%29.jpg/330px-Aft_%28PSF%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_and_starboard"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Tapisserie_bato1.jpg/500px-Tapisserie_bato1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Tapisserie_bato1.jpg/500px-Tapisserie_bato1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Image from the Bayeux Tapestry showing a longship with a steering oar on the starboard side.[4]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATapisserie_bato1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Maschinenfahrzeug_%28nachts%29.png/500px-Maschinenfahrzeug_%28nachts%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Maschinenfahrzeug_%28nachts%29.png/500px-Maschinenfahrzeug_%28nachts